course: dictionary
lesson: 5661
title: Lithium: a light metal in batteries
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Lithium is a science word, and you will see it on phones, laptops and electric cars. When you meet it, read the words around it. «Phones need metals like lithium, cobalt, copper and gold from mines.» Lithium sits in a list of metals, so it must be a metal too.
explain: «In a rechargeable phone battery, lithium moves from one side to the other as you use it.» The words battery and charging tell you lithium is used to store power. Swap in your meaning to check: a light, soft metal that helps a battery hold power still makes sense.
explain: The sentence «If one swells, gets hot or smells, tell an adult, and never pierce or crush it» shows that lithium batteries need care. The clues are swells, gets hot and smells, so a damaged battery can be dangerous.
fact: Lithium is a chemical element with the symbol Li.
fact: Lithium is a very light, soft, silvery metal.
fact: Lithium is used in rechargeable batteries for phones, laptops and electric cars.
fact: «Lithium-ion» batteries can get very hot or catch fire if they are damaged.
fact: Phones contain metals dug from mines, so an old phone is worth recycling.
exercise: What is lithium? | A type of plastic bag | A bright red liquid | A kind of wood | *A very light, soft, silvery metal
exercise: «Lithium batteries in phones, tablets and e-scooters hold a lot of energy.» What is lithium used for? | Paper for school books | *Rechargeable batteries for phones and laptops | Wooden toys
exercise: «If one swells, gets hot or smells, tell an adult.» What should you do with a damaged lithium battery? | Pierce it with a pin | Crush it to make it smaller | *Tell an adult | Leave it on the bed to charge
test: «Your phone also holds metals dug from mines, such as lithium, cobalt, copper and gold.» Which one of these is a metal from the list? | Plastic | Cotton | Glass | *Cobalt
test: «Lithium-ion batteries can catch fire if damaged, so they should not be left charging on a bed.» Where should a lithium battery not be left charging? | *On a bed | On a shelf | In a cool box
exam: «An electric car's battery pack is thousands of small lithium cells joined together.» What is lithium in this sentence? | A type of road | A school subject | A kind of car | *A metal used in the cells of the battery
